        "item_what_is": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What does organic cotton mean?",
            "text": "<p>Organic cotton is grown without synthetic pesticides, synthetic fertilizers, or genetically modified seeds. It's a farming method, not a fabric type — the cotton itself is still cotton, just grown differently.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        },
        "item_gots": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What GOTS certification means",
            "text": "<p>The Global Organic Textile Standard (GOTS) is one of the strictest independent certifications for organic textiles. GOTS-certified fabric requires a minimum of <strong>70% certified organic fibres</strong>, rising to <strong>95%</strong> for products carrying the GOTS label. It also prohibits toxic pesticides, formaldehyde, and heavy metals, and sets requirements for fair wages and safe working conditions across the supply chain.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        },
        "item_living_crafts": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Living Crafts",
            "text": "<p>Living Crafts has held <strong>continuous GOTS certification since 2009</strong>, certified by Control Union. Their organic cotton is sourced mainly from India, where cultivation and processing happen close together to reduce transport emissions.</p>",
            "heading_color": "secondary"
          }
        },
